            <ArticleTitle>An unusual case of a sore throat and otalgia in a 4-year-old boy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>277-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A sore throat, otalgia, and snoring are the common symptoms seen in children presenting to an otorhinolaryngological clinic. Sometimes, however, these symptoms may be suggestive of an aggressive malignancy. We present a rare case of Burkitt's lymphoma of the tonsil in a young child, which initially manifested as a sore throat and otalgia.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
